			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Terminal serialization/revival, fill IPC gaps\n\nComplete the terminal window-reload persistence cycle and close multiple VS Code Workbench IPC compatibility gaps:\n\n**Terminal state persistence (window reload):**\n- Add `SerializeTerminalState` — snapshot all active PTYs to `ISerializedTerminalState[]` with `shellLaunchConfig`, `processDetails`, and replay metadata, called by `localPty:serializeTerminalState` just before reload.\n- Add `ReviveTerminalProcesses` — respawn shells from the snapshot array, forwarding each entry to `TerminalCreate` and emitting `sky://terminal/create` for the xterm panel. Skips entries with an empty executable.\n- Wire `localPty:getRevivedPtyNewId` to `GetNextTerminalIdentifier()` (no longer a no-op) so the workbench pre-allocates collision-free IDs before revival.\n\n**Configuration/Theme IPC completeness:**\n- Alias `configuration:lookup` → `ConfigurationGet` — needed by `IConfigurationService.getValue(key)` in the Workbench singleton.\n- Implement `configuration:inspect` — returns `{value, default, user, workspace, workspaceFolder, memory}` with the current effective value in both `value` and `default`, null for all scope overrides (correct for Land where no user/workspace JSON overrides exist).\n- Alias `themes:getColorTheme` → `ThemesGetActive` — `IThemeService.getColorTheme()` Workbench channel method.\n- Extend `ThemesGetActive` response with numeric `ColorThemeKind` enum (`type`: 1-4) and `semanticHighlighting: false` so tokenization and colour-picker internals have the expected shape.\n\n**Dialog unwrapping for Wind consumption:**\n- `UserInterface.ShowOpenDialog` — unwrap `{canceled, filePaths}` envelope to bare `string[]` so Wind's `Array.isArray(result)` guard finds the paths.\n- `UserInterface.ShowSaveDialog` — unwrap `{canceled, filePath}` envelope to bare path string so Wind's `typeof result === \"string\"` guard succeeds.\n\n**Path format fix in sandbox config:**\n- Convert `appRoot`, `homeDir`, `tmpDir`, `userDataDir`, `backupPath` from `file://` URLs to plain OS filesystem paths. VS Code's `URI.file(path)` receives these via `AbstractNativeEnvironmentService` and double-encodes a `file://` string, producing broken `path.join` bases.\n\n**Provider registration for VS Code ≥1.87 APIs:**\n- Add `register_inline_completion_item_provider`, `register_inline_edit_provider`, `register_multi_document_highlight_provider`, `register_mapped_edits_provider`, `register_document_paste_edit_provider`, `register_document_drop_edit_provider` — each wires through `CreateProviderEffect` into the existing ProviderRegistration map so the Language Feature dispatch layer can proxy `$provideXxx` requests back to Cocoon.\n\n**Terminal show/hide via gRPC provider path:**\n- Wire `$terminal:show`/`$terminal:hide` and `Terminal.Show`/`Terminal.Hide` through `TerminalProvider` — Cocoon's window namespace shim calls these when extensions invoke `terminal.show(preserveFocus)` or `terminal.hide()`, and both call sites now share one implementation.\n\n**Debug configuration provider cleanup:**\n- Add gRPC notification `unregister_debug_configuration_provider` with `UnregisterDebugConfigurationProvider` handler — mirrors `UnregisterDebugAdapter` for the DebugConfiguration slot, invoked when an extension disposes a `vscode.debug.registerDebugConfigurationProvider` registration.\n\n**Stub-ack additions:**\n- Add `log:registerLogger`/`log:createLogger` alongside the existing `logger:*` stubs — VS Code 1.87+ calls both prefixes and was crashing on every boot with \"registered but no dispatch arm\".\n\n13 files changed, 479 insertions, 23 deletions.",
